{{!< default}}
{{!-- Full-page security feed — the widget as a destination, not a sidebar block.

     Ghost resolves a page's template as page-:slug.hbs -> custom-*.hbs -> page.hbs, so
     this file is picked up automatically by a page whose slug is "secfeed". It renders
     the same block partials/featured-row.hbs puts beside the featured post, with
     `full=true` for the three things a page changes: the frame stops being a bounded
     box, the document scrolls instead of the list, and the island is asked for the
     maximum number of advisories instead of the administrator's `sec_feed_items`.
     See partials/sec-feed.hbs for the contract and which half of it each mode owns.

     `locale` is passed at this level, never inside {{#page}}: a context-changing block
     drops a partial's hash arguments (see partials/page-body.hbs), so a match on
     `locale` nested in {{#page}} would always take the English branch. The Spanish
     counterpart is a file like this one extending default-es.hbs, selected in the
     page's Template setting — the same remedy custom-page-es.hbs documents.

     This is a *minified* frontend, not a replacement for the service's own app: the
     footer link still hands over to https://security-feed.sredevops.org for search and
     the full archive. --}}

{{#page}}
    {{!-- @page.show_title_and_feature_image is the per-page toggle in the editor.
         Honouring it is why this is not simply an unconditional <h1>. --}}
    {{#if @page.show_title_and_feature_image}}
    <h1 class="text-4xl text-strong font-bold mb-4">{{title}}</h1>
    {{> "feature-image"}}
    {{/if}}
    {{#if custom_excerpt}}
    <p class="text-muted text-lg mb-8">{{custom_excerpt}}</p>
    {{/if}}
{{/page}}

<div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto pb-12">
    {{> "sec-feed" locale="en" full=true}}
</div>
